{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-14T04:31:19.556Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9d7f970542d8df5a0a6bdb3b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1713","claim:pm-gh1719","lineage:pm-gh1713","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1713+pm-gh1719","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1713","claim:pm-gh1719","lineage:pm-gh1713","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-womkyw"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"pm copy writes a new item without evaluating workflow policies, while create, update, delete, restore and imports all run enforceWorkflowMutation"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found while implementing pm-gh1719 (2026-11-14). Every item writer runs enforceWorkflowMutation before persistence and records its decisions in the history entry context (workflow_policies): create, the item-store mutate and delete paths, restore, and the package import adapter. runCopy in src/sdk/lifecycle/copy.ts writes the copied item and its op create history entry without it, so a workflow policy that refuses or annotates creation (for example a per-type creation rule or a required-field policy) is bypassed by copying an existing item, and the copy's history carries no workflow_policies decisions. pm-gh1719 added the missing beforeMutation guard call to copy but left workflow policy enforcement unchanged to keep that change scoped. Proposal: call enforceWorkflowMutation in runCopy with operation create, before null and after the copied document, and record its decisions in the history context exactly as create does. Duplicate check: searched copy workflow policy enforce bypass; pm-mj42og (closed) delivered the policy engine without naming copy."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:sdk","copy","governance","workflow-policy"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-14T04:31:19.556Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-14T04:31:19.556Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"pm copy evaluates the workspace workflow policies with operation create and refuses a copy that create would refuse; The copy's history entry records the workflow_policies decisions like a create; A spec proves a refusing policy blocks both create and copy"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-33cw"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Copy is judged by the same workflow policies as create"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Copy bypasses workflow policies entirely"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1719","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-14T04:31:19.556Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-mj42og","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-14T04:31:19.556Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_